{
  "_purpose": "Single source of truth for every event the property sends (Finding 9 fix). scripts/generate-blueprint.mjs emits one payload data element per entry from ONE template, plus the rule that sends it. Adding a tracked interaction = adding an entry here and re-running the generator; hand-editing generated payloads is prohibited.",
  "_analyticsTransport": "Per the audit's Fix 1/2 guidance (deck slide 28), payloads use the Web SDK `data.__adobe.analytics` object (the documented AppMeasurement-migration path) \u2014 no XDM schema required while Amazon News has no AEP subscription. eVar/prop/event numbers are byte-for-byte the source property's mappings.",
  "_acdlEventSentinel": {
    "value": "CONFIRM-VIA-EXPORT",
    "meaning": "The source workbook (Launch Inspector) does not export WHICH adobeDataLayer event name each Datalayer Push Listener listens for. Run scripts/export-current.mjs against the existing AboutAmazon-US property to produce catalog/acdl-events.overrides.json with the real names; generate-blueprint.mjs refuses to emit a publishable blueprint while any acdlEvent is unresolved.",
    "calibration": "Verified 2026-07-29 against the old property's 'Global CTA Button Tracking' rule: the ACDL event type is displayed 'Data Pushed'; per rule record the 'Listen to: Specific Event' -> 'Event / Key to register for' value plus the Time scope radio (All/Future/Past). First captured: CTAButtonClicked, Time scope All. Site convention appears PascalCase \u2014 do not infer the rest; read each rule."
  },
